{title: 493 - Fill My Cup, Lord}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #493 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 493}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]Like the woman at the [Bdim6]well I was [F7]seeking
For things that could not satis[Bb]fy:
And then I [Bb7]heard my Savior [Eb]speaking:
“Draw from my [F7]well that never shall run [Bb]dry”.
Fill [Eb]my cup [Bb]Lord, I lift it [F7]up, Lord!
Come and quench this thirsting of my [Bb]soul;
[F7]Bread of [Bb]heaven, [Bb7]Feed me till I [F7]want [Bb]no [Cm7]more–
Fill my [F7]cup, [Cm7]fill it [F7]up and make me [Bb]whole!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Bb]Fill my cup [Bdim6]Lord, I lift [F7]it up, Lord!
[Bb]Come and quench this thirsting of my soul;
[Bb7]Bread of heaven, Feed me [Eb]till I want no more--
[F7]Fill my cup, fill it [Bb]up and make me whole!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]There are millions [Bdim6]in this world [F7]who are craving
[Bb]The pleasures earthly things afford;
[Bb7]But none can [Eb]match the wondrous treasure
[F7]That I find in [Bb]Jesus Christ my Lord.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]So, my brother, [Bdim6]if the things [F7]this world gave you
[Bb]Leave hungers that won't pass away,
[Bb7]My blessed Lord will [Eb]come and save you,
[F7]If you kneel to [Bb]Him and humbly pray:
{end_of_verse}
